{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Migrate the endpoint to node2 on TCP 4180 while preserving health, identity, and two-worker SO_REUSEPORT behavior.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before migration, the endpoint returned the expected health and identity and exposed both workers. After cutover and node2's restart, legacy-netapp.service.lan resolved to 10.100.66.11, returned legacy-netapp-ok and migration-cohort-44, distributed requests across workers 1 and 2, and had two sockets bound to 10.100.66.11:4180.","evidence_ids":["legacy-external-flow","legacy-reuseport-workers","cmd-fc3adfc535534be3","cmd-407935bdd4184a7a","cmd-7bf05fc75ee04598","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Expose the migrated service only on node2's application LAN.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both listener sockets were bound only to node2's application-LAN address 10.100.66.11. Independent requests to its client/management-LAN address 10.100.108.11 failed before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1a9bb0451a684b55","cmd-407935bdd4184a7a","cmd-7bf05fc75ee04598","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the legacy stateful, rate-limited firewall policy on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 retained the legacy INPUT hook, established/related acceptance, invalid-state drop, application-interface and source-CIDR restriction, 120/second burst-240 NEW-connection limit, rate-limited logging, and final TCP-reset rejection. The policy and service survived node2's reboot, and counters showed both accepted and rejected traffic.","evidence_ids":["legacy-firewall-policy","cmd-0fdb89a8516a431b","cmd-407935bdd4184a7a","cmd-fa485a4a3ed64f22"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Retire node1's listener and application-specific firewall policy.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1's two workers and firewall service were disabled and stopped, the INPUT jump and LEGACY_NETAPP chain were removed, and port 4180 had no