es","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material migration outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: node1 changed from boot ID 6adec1ab-4f89-41a1-92c6-64828eb08932 to 4c32ecff-9dc0-4b5d-b19d-f9eb415eb12f, and node2 changed from 28ae5f98-80ff-424c-9f6f-523320557628 to 1878ac34-13bd-4aa0-98a9-24be6d95f0eb. Each had a restart acknowledgement and direct recovered-state checks, and the fixed lifecycle boot identities corroborate the transitions.","limitations":["The executor final report and selected-evidence set were unavailable, so this assessment relies on the complete command timeline and fixed lifecycle snapshots.","Preservation of all unrelated configuration was not established through an exhaustive filesystem inventory; it is supported by the complete mutation trace, targeted hashes, package checks, and failed-service observations.","The firewall rules and traffic counters directly establish the retained rate-limited policy, but no controlled saturation test measured the limit boundary itself.","The after-executor collector recorded a CancelledError lifecycle outcome, although its per-node snapshots were successfully captured and coherent."]}
